      "notes": "for brushing"
    },
    {
      "name": "peanuts",
      "amount": "1/4 cup",
      "notes": "chopped, for garnish"
    },
    {
      "name": "fish sauce",
      "amount": "2 tablespoons",
      "notes": "for serving (optional)"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Mix coconut milk, coriander powder, brown sugar, lemongrass, and galangal in a bowl. Heat the tava griddle to 400°F. Thread fish sticks onto skewers. Brush skewers with vegetable oil. Grill skewers for 4 minutes on each side, or until golden brown. Serve with turkish delight, peanuts, and fish sauce (if using). Garnish with chopped peanuts and lemongrass. Let rest for at least 15 minutes before serving. Enjoy immediately after resting to maximize hangover-curing properties."
